A2  - Bressler, S. L., Bressler, Canales, A. F., Gomez, D. M., Maffet, C. R., Canales, Gaillard, R., Dehaene, S., Adam, C., Clemenceau, S., Hasboun, D., Baulac, M., et al., Gaillard, Hameroff, S., Hameroff, Hobson, J. A., Pace-Schott, E. F., Stickgold, R., Hobson, John, E. R., Prichep, L. S., Kox, W., Valdes-Sosa, P., Bosch-Bayard, J., Aubert, E., et al., John, Pockett, S., Bold, G. E. J., Freeman, W. J., Pockett, Rodriguez, E., George, N., Lachaux, J. P., Martinerie, J., Renault, B., Varela, F. J., Rodriguez, Roelfsema, P. R., Engel, A. K., Konig, P., Singer, W., Roelfsema, Sewards, T. V., Sewards, M. A., Sewards, Shadlen, M. N., Movshon, J. A., Shadlen, Srinivasen, T., Russell, D. P., Edelman, G. M., Tononi, G., Srinivasen, Steriade, M., Amzica, F., Contreras, D., Steriade, Steriade, M., Contreras, D., Amzica, F., Steriade, Stopfer, M., Bhagavan, S., Smith, B. H., Laurent, G., Stopfer, Tallon-Baudry, C., Tallon-Baudry, Trujillo, L. T., Peterson, M. A., Kaszniak, A. W., Allen, J. J. B., Trujillo, Uhlhaas, P. J., Roux, F., Singer, W., Haenschel, C., Sireteanu, R., Rodriguez, E., Uhlhaas, Vanderwolf, C. H., Vanderwolf, Varela, F., Lachaux, J. P., Rodriguez, E., Martinerie, J., Varela, Wyart, V., Tallon-Baudry, C., Wyart
Y1  - 2009//
N2  - Power density spectra and phase synchrony measurements were taken from intracranial electrode grids implanted in epileptic subjects. Comparisons were made between data from the waking state and from the period of unconsciousness immediately following a generalized tonic-clonic seizure. Power spectra in the waking state resembled coloured noise. Power spectra in the unconscious state resembled coloured noise from 1 to about 5 Hz, but at higher frequencies changed in two out of three subjects to resemble white noise. This boosted unconscious gamma power to a higher level than conscious gamma power. For both gamma and beta passbands, synchrony measurements showed more widespread phase synchrony in the unconscious than the conscious state. We conclude that neither gamma activity per se nor phase synchrony per se are neural correlates of consciousness. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
