Y1  - 1994//
N2  - Demonstrates how the dynamic measure based on the largest local Lyapunov exponent can be applied for the detection of the changes of the chaoticity of the brain processes measured in EEG and magnetoencephalogram experiments. An algorithm is presented for computation of chaoticity that is especially useful for nonstationary signals. Moreover, the idea is introduced that chaoticity is able to detect, locally in time, critical jumps (phase-transitionlike phenomena) in the human brain, as well as the information flow through the cortex. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
