T1  - Correlations between ERP parameters and intelligence: A reconsideration.
A1  - Jausovec, Norbert
A1  - Jausovec, Ksenija

Y1  - 2000//
N2  - Investigated differences in event related potential (ERP) parameters related to intelligence. 74 18-21 yr olds (Intelligence range 73-135), of average creativity passively listened to 2 tones and performed 2 auditory, and 2 visual oddball tasks while their EEG was recorded. The approximate entropy parameters, peak latencies and amplitudes were determined. The correlation coefficients indicate that in the attended conditions, the more intelligent individuals showed more regular ERP waveforms than less intelligent individuals. It was further found that less intelligent individuals showed increased P300 latencies and reduced amplitudes. The differences were explained with a more specific engagement of neural networks in more intelligent individuals. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
