T1  - Nonlinear analysis of sleep EEG data in schizophrenia: Calculation of the principal Lyapunov exponent.
A1  - Roscke, Joachim
A1  - Fell, Jurgen
A1  - Beckmann, Peter

Y1  - 1995//
N2  - Examined whether there are any differences between the principal Lyapunov exponents of the sleep EEG in schizophrenic patients compared with healthy controls and whether the calculation of the Lyapunov exponent L1 provides clues about the deficient information processing in schizophrenia. L1 was calculated for sleep EEG segments of 13 acute schizophrenic patients and 13 control Ss that corresponded to Sleep Stages I-IV and REM for the lead positions Cz and Pz. During REM sleep, for both electrode positions, L1 was significantly increased in schizophrenic patients compared with control Ss. This finding points to altered nonlinear brain dynamics during REM sleep in schizophrenia. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
