A1  - Roschke, J
A1  - Fell, J
A1  - Beckmann, P

Y1  - 1995//
N2  - Investigated nonlinear properties of sleep electroencephalographic (EEG) data to elucidate functional alterations other than those obtained from classical sleep analysis. For 15 inpatients (aged 23-61 yrs) and 13 healthy matched controls the principal Lyapunov exponents were computed. The exponents computed were L1 of EEG segments corresponding to sleep stages I, II, III, IV, and rapid eye movement, according to A. Rechtschaffen and A. Kales (1968). Results showed decreased values of L1 during sleep stage IV in depressed Ss compared with controls. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
