T1  - Strange attractors, chaotic behavior and informational aspects of sleep EEG data.
A1  - Roschke, J

Y1  - 1992//
N2  - To perform a nonlinear dimensional analysis of sleep EEG, the author applied an algorithm proposed to calculate the correlation dimension D2 of different sleep stages. D2 characterizes the dynamics of sleep EEG, estimates the degree of freedom, and describes the complexity of the signal under study. An attempt was made to correlate dimensionality analysis and informational aspects of sleep EEG. Information processing by the brain during different sleep stages of 12 healthy men under the influence of lorazepam and in 11 adult unmedicated acute schizophrenic inpatients was estimated. Results suggest an alteration of the CNS workload during psychosis, which may injure the brain's ability of correct information processing, and therefore may be an expression of the pathophysiological mechanism underlying schizophrenia. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
